                  "code": "UPDATE_SUMMARY_WITH_NEXT_CHUNK",
                  "id": "1776031005404",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1776031005404_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are updating a summary of a customer service chat using the next chunk of transcript.\n\nTreat the existing summary as a draft that must stay strictly grounded in the chat. You are also given a small handoff object that carries unresolved context from the previous chunk.\n\nReturn only a JSON object with exactly these top-level fields:\n- \"summary\": the revised summary text\n- \"chunkHandoff\": the refreshed handoff object for the next chunk\n\nRules:\n- Use only the existing summary, the existing chunkHandoff, and the new transcript chunk provided below.\n- Keep the summary written from the customer's point of view, in second person, as if the customer asked for the summary.\n- Prefer phrasing such as \"you contacted the agent\" and \"your KX 250\" instead of third-person wording such as \"the customer contacted the agent\" or \"his KX 250\".\n- Preserve a fact from the existing summary only if it is still consistent with the new chunk.\n- Add a new fact only if it is explicitly supported by the new chunk.\n- Remove or correct any statement that is unsupported, vague, or contradicted by the new chunk.\n- Treat chunkHandoff.pendingTopics as high-priority unresolved context from the previous chunk.\n- Pay special attention to questions asked at the end of the previous chunk and answers that appear at the beginning of the new chunk. These are often part of the same exchange.\n- If the first message or first few messages in the new chunk appear to respond to, explain, continue, or resolve a pending topic from chunkHandoff, treat them as connected unless the transcript clearly indicates otherwise.\n- Prefer linking an opening explanation in the new chunk to the most recent pending topic when the subject matter is similar.\n- Do not keep a topic marked unresolved if the new chunk provides a direct explanation, instructions, answer, or resolution for it.\n- When the new chunk resolves a pending topic from chunkHandoff, update the summary so that topic is no longer treated as unresolved and remove it from pendingTopics.\n- Refresh chunkHandoff so it includes only unresolved topics that remain pending after considering the new chunk.\n- Keep pendingTopics small and focused on the most relevant unresolved items.\n- Do not infer broader business context or invent scenario details.\n- Do not introduce topics such as shipping, refunds, billing, addresses, delivery, orders, warranties, or follow-up commitments unless they are explicitly present in the provided text.\n- Keep the result focused on what was actually said: the issue, suggestions, actions taken, resolution status, and any explicit next step.\n- If the new chunk is small or informal, update the summary conservatively rather than expanding it.\n- Keep the updated summary to about {{$context.$variables.summarySizeWords}} words or less.\n\nExisting summary:\n{{$context.$variables.rollingSummary}}\n\nExisting chunkHandoff:\n{{$context.$variables.chunkHandoff}}\n\nNext chat transcript chunk:\n{{$context.$nodes.MULTICHUNK_WITH_SUMMARY_LOGIC.currentItem.transcript}}"
                    }
                  ],
